<resources>
    <string name="game__bluff__title">Bluff!</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__tagline">Fool your friends</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__howto__1">Three rounds, three ways to lie: finish a saying, crack an impossible fact, then a final with no truth at all.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__howto__2">Write a fake answer on your phone. Know the real ending of the saying? Type it: you score right away.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__howto__3">Find the real answer among the fakes. Nobody knows who wrote what until the vote is over.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__howto__4">Score twice: +100 for the truth, +60 for every friend who falls for your lie. In the final, the most convincing answer wins big.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__goal__title">The goal</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__goal__body">Fool your friends, and don\'t get fooled. Best with 4 players or more.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__round1__title">Round 1: Finish the saying</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__round1__body">Type the ending. If your first answer is the real one, you get +150 at once and sit that vote out. If not, your answer becomes a fake on the board.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__round2__title">Round 2: Impossible but true</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__round2__body">A very hard but real fact. Write a fake that sounds truer than the truth. Points ×2.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__writing__title">Writing</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__writing__body">%1$s s, max 60 characters, in the same alphabet as the prompt. Too close to the real answer? You\'ll be asked for another one, and finding the truth on that prompt won\'t score. Stuck? \"Help me\" suggests a lie (a small fee comes off what it earns).</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__voting__title">Voting</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__voting__body">Vote for the answer you think is true, never your own. Like up to 2 answers you find funny.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__points__title">Points</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__points__body">Truth: +100 (round 2: +200). Each player fooled: +60 (round 2: +120). Each like: +10.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__final__title">Final: No truth</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__final__body">There is no right answer. Write the most convincing answer, then vote for the one that sounds most true. Each vote: +150. Most votes: +400. Nobody sees who voted for what.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__house__title">House lies</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__house__body">With few players, the game adds its own lies. Don\'t fall for them!</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__same__title">Same lie?</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__same__body">It shows once and the authors share the points.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__host__title">Host</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__rules__host__body">The host can skip a prompt or hide an answer; if the host hides the real one, the prompt is cancelled and nobody scores on it.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__coach__round_intro">New round, new way to lie. Read the rule on the card.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__coach__writing">Write a lie that sounds true. Same shape as the hint.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__coach__voting">Pick the answer you believe. Never your own.</string>
    <string name="game__bluff__coach__reveal">Watch who fooled whom.</string>
